{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say each contract must cover consecutive months starting from the beginning of the period, do you mean that every contract must start in month 1 (so the only possible contracts are a 1-month, 2-month, 3-month, or 4-month contract all beginning in month 1), or do you mean contracts can start in any month as long as they cover consecutive months (e.g., a 2-month contract could cover months 2-3 or months 3-4)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the start month of contracts, presenting two mutually exclusive interpretations as a single choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any other mutual exclusion rules between different contract lengths (for example, does choosing a 3-month contract exclude any other length, or does choosing a 2-month contract exclude any other length)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of other mutual exclusion rules between contract lengths. The parenthetical examples illustrate the type of information requested but do not constitute separate independent questions."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since each warehouse has unlimited capacity and contracts can cover the full required area or part of it, can you rent multiple warehouses of the same contract length in parallel (for example, two separate 2-month contracts, each covering part of the area), or is at most one warehouse of each contract length allowed?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether multiple warehouses of the same contract length can be rented in parallel or if there is a limit of one per length."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since each warehouse has unlimited capacity, does the area requirement for each month need to be met exactly, or is it acceptable to have the total rented area exceed the required area in some months (i.e., is over-renting allowed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the area constraint is an equality or an inequality (allowing over-renting)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since each warehouse has unlimited capacity and the area must be met exactly each month, is the decision variable the area (in ㎡) rented from each chosen contract length, with the constraint that the sum of areas from all active contracts in a given month equals the required area for that month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound clarification question asking for confirmation of the proposed decision variable definition and its associated constraint. Although it contains multiple clauses, it seeks a single yes/no confirmation of the modeling structure, making it one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the total cost simply the sum of (area rented from each contract length) × (fee per 100㎡ for that length) / 100",
    "is the objective to minimize this total cost over the 4 months?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two distinct clarification requests: one regarding the calculation method for total cost and another regarding the optimization objective. A user could confirm the cost formula without confirming the objective, or vice versa."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the decision variables (areas rented from each contract length) continuous, or must they be integer values (e.g., in whole ㎡ or whole 100㎡ units)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the domain (continuous vs. integer) of the decision variables."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the mutual exclusion rule (if a 4-month contract is chosen, no 1-month contract may be chosen), does \"chosen\" mean that the area rented from the 4-month contract is strictly greater than zero, and \"no 1-month contract may be chosen\" means the area rented from the 1-month contract must be exactly zero?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the specific definition of 'chosen' and 'not chosen' within the mutual exclusion rule. Although it contains two clauses, they are linked by 'and' to define the same logical condition for the rule, making it one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the area variables are continuous and the mutual exclusion rule states that if the 4-month contract area is strictly greater than zero, the 1-month contract area must be exactly zero, is the reverse also true (i.e., if the 1-month contract area is zero, the 4-month contract area can be anything, including zero)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the logical converse of a specific constraint."
